# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables.
#
# Anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, `debug` matches a path segment
# of that name anywhere in the tree, which is how .agents/skills/debug/ stayed
# uncommitted from the founding commit until slice S071 while sitting in
# skills-lock.json the whole time. Cargo writes to target/debug, which the next
# line already covers.
/debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Node and the documentation site (specification sections 21.3 and 22)
node_modules
.next
out
.turbo
site/test-results/
site/playwright-report/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment and secrets
.env
.env.local

# Capture output. Capture files can carry addresses, and in some titles session
# identifiers, so nothing written by a live run is ever committed by accident.
# Test fixtures are the exception and live under fixtures/, which is tracked.
#
# Deliberately unanchored: an earlier path defect wrote sessions to
# docs/captures/ instead of the repository root, where only the *.pcapng rule
# caught them and the socket log and manifest were left tracked. Match the
# directory name anywhere rather than relying on it landing where intended.
captures/
recon-session/
*.fcapng
*.pcapng
*.pcap
sockets.jsonl
processes.jsonl
!fixtures/**/*.fcapng
!fixtures/**/*.pcapng
!fixtures/**/*.pcap
# Committed capture goldens also live beside the tests that assert them (slice
# S14's CLI end-to-end goldens), so the same exception applies there.
!crates/**/tests/goldens/*.fcapng
!crates/**/tests/goldens/*.pcapng

# npcap Software Development Kit. Acquired at build time, never vendored
# (specification section 20.2). If a local build drops it here, it stays out
# of the repository.
/npcap-sdk
/vendor/npcap*

# Per-agent skill views.
#
# The portable, vendored skill content lives in .agents/skills/ and is
# committed, along with skills-lock.json. Codex reads .agents/skills/ directly,
# so it needs nothing further. Claude Code and Cursor read their own
# directories, and the skills CLI populates those with machine-local symlinks
# carrying absolute paths, which are meaningless on another machine.
#
# So: ignore the contents of those directories, but keep Spec Kit's own
# generated speckit-* skills tracked, since those are real files that every
# contributor needs and that the spec-kit CLI regenerates deterministically.
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/speckit-*
/.cursor/skills/*
!/.cursor/skills/speckit-*
/.github/skills/

/.claude/launch.json
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Spec Kit local state.
# feature.json is a per-branch pointer to the active slice. Committing it makes
# every concurrent pull request conflict on it; the durable artifact is the
# specs/<feature>/ directory itself.
/.specify/feature.json
# active-slice.md is the per-slice narrative the agent-context updater rewrites
# every slice. Kept local so it adds no pointer-only diff noise to AGENTS.md.
/.specify/active-slice.md

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
